<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Microsoft says consumer products 'fully recovered', business services improving</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a546eada68c081708c3cc34440f5c8e82cfa9856c8dbab5f5afcbaab1b605be9</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:07:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20261114-microsoft-says-consumer-products-fully-recovered-business-services-improving--42e4ac49238f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261114-microsoft-says-consumer-products-fully-recovered-business-services-improving" /><summary type="html">Resolution seems in sight on Saturday following confirmation by tech giant Microsoft on Friday that services had ​fully ‌recovered ⁠across ‌Teams, Outlook, Copilot and ⁠other applications, ​ending a ‌global outage ‌that ​crippled online communications across businesses and ​governments ​for ​over 24 hours. The US homeland security chief confirmed there was 'no Microsoft link' to the US air stoppage.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>FAA lifts nationwide ground stop on all US flights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:429f4713a55b6a9f2a79c6e435a3b573f417f6a6c748a4e0a16e2336516942ad</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T02:50:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-faa-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-on-all-us-flights--8fca9e8bb835.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-faa-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-on-all-us-flights" /><summary type="html">The United States on Friday lifted an hours-long ground stop at the nation's airports, with top officials explaining that the disruption was not due to a cyberattack or a sweeping Microsoft outage.</summary></entry><entry><title>US flights resume after nationwide ground stop lifted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5492df9acb0d9e66d8c1dfcd020f31d6c4f86a8f36df546fcc7cca74043424bf</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T02:35:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation--ee4c7a228fe5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation" /><summary type="html">The United States on Friday lifted an hours-long ground stop at the nation's airports, with top officials explaining that the disruption was not due to a cyberattack or a sweeping Microsoft outage. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said that US airspace was now "opened up," and blamed "old hardware" for the travel chaos.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Gambia's Adama Barrow seeks third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c55cdd0724e3448b75f47ad6cd18c536b251a668d03a09dd16dbfa0daba18b0</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:46:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gambia-s-adama-barrow-seeks-third-term--167d5d5b0803.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gambia-s-adama-barrow-seeks-third-term" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, Gambia's electoral commission has announced the five official candidates for the country's upcoming presidential election. President Adama Barrow is seeking a third term. Tensions continue to rise in Ethiopia following the federal government's appointment of a new head of the Western Tigray region. And the Dakar Youth Olympic Games come to a close after two weeks of intense competition.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>France among five major powers to represent EU in Ukraine talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27a31c26f4ea8d970554d9c84ba1f40fda475c5ed26947a28328c93b51316595</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:38:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-europe-to-send-diplomats-from-across-the-continent-to-ukraine-peace-talks--44eded81bb78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-europe-to-send-diplomats-from-across-the-continent-to-ukraine-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">European Council President Antonio Costa on Friday said that Brussels will send diplomats from the bloc and five countries, including the UK, France, Germany, Italy and Poland, to upcoming Ukraine talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 US flight authority orders national ground stop over air traffic control 'communication issue'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:283cceac1eb26f9bd2b04779f3bdfc5e9e0c16bd42a60b2cb869e03a596695a3</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:29:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-flight-authority-orders-national-ground-stop-over-air-traffic-control-communication-issu--bea6c8926b2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-flight-authority-orders-national-ground-stop-over-air-traffic-control-communication-issue" /></entry><entry><title>US flight authority orders national ground stop over air traffic control 'communication issue'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5a0e0e8895b6eb2d087f6882629eab591c71e38baf0b268728b57106a3293f7</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:27:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-flight-authority-orders-national-ground-stop-over-air-traffic-control-communication-issu--bea6c8926b2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-flight-authority-orders-national-ground-stop-over-air-traffic-control-communication-issue" /><summary type="html">The US flight authority on Friday halted flights across the nation due to what US Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said was a communication issue affecting the country's air traffic control centres.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey and Qatar pledge unified stance against attacks in mutual defence pact</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a135df455f9afb6e082d57edbf03edf01cbce2bb208b03c50a9d3527b2c03138</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T20:06:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261113-turkey-and-qatar-pledge-unified-stance-against-attacks-in-mutual-defence-pact--78a12542999d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261113-turkey-and-qatar-pledge-unified-stance-against-attacks-in-mutual-defence-pact" /><summary type="html">Turkey and Qatar signed a mutual defence agreement Friday, pledging a unified response to any attack on either country, the two leaders said in a joint statement. The defence pact follows the Mecca Joint Defence Agreement signed by Turkey, Pakistan and Saudi Arabia in August.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>The Downfall of AI’s ‘Rock Star’ Boss, Ukraine: Who speaks for Europe? Protests &amp; Presidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb8bc93a08c46f6d24d65b2fa73ac222f1ac5dc2dfb0aef5b347ec659b3d8f0d</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:46:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261113-the-downfall-of-ai-s-rock-star-boss-ukraine-who-speak-for-europe-protests-presidents--795148188632.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261113-the-downfall-of-ai-s-rock-star-boss-ukraine-who-speak-for-europe-protests-presidents" /><summary type="html">On The World This Week with Gavin Lee, our panel distills the breaking news and global stories of the past 7 days into 45 minutes. 
 
Ukraine: Who will speak for Europe?
 
In a week thats seen the first direct talks between Ukraine and Russia since February, with the US in the room and the Europeans relegated to the lobby according to Moscow. A new ‘European Security Architecture’ is discussed.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Hurry up and wait: Europe wants a place at the table, ‘must make up its mind’ over Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9069d4cfdd78e4ca09244a77d118841a3fb3ab87dd6eb29a70f7315d3f24072f</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:03:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261113-hurry-up-and-wait-europe-wants-a-place-at-the-table-must-make-up-its-mind-over-ukraine--0ede6861b758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261113-hurry-up-and-wait-europe-wants-a-place-at-the-table-must-make-up-its-mind-over-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Gavin Lee is pleased to welcome Alexander Titov, Lecturer in Modern European History at Queen's University Belfast and a specialist on Russia. He's joined us to discuss high-level meetings in Abu Dhabi, Dublin and the prospects for ending the war in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>What we know about China's military exercises around Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:baeb19b71b455701ce1167dc7f7fbfd5e910a59a8518d09aad62523106affc75</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T18:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261113-chinese-army-military-exercises-taiwan--5fe8dc54e260.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261113-chinese-army-military-exercises-taiwan" /><summary type="html">China has been carrying out major military drills around Taiwan since early November. But contrary to some claims on social media, Beijing's armed forces have not actually implemented a blockade on the island; they just simulated it.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'We have done all our homework' to get EU candidate status: Kosovo's PM Albin Kurti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3174e878f393d501ba619391bd648ea7a4c5cd4f3127d12a1df120c156eeda6</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:46:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261113-we-have-done-all-our-homework-to-get-eu-candidate-status-kosovo-s-pm-albin-kurti--597ebf8d6a3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261113-we-have-done-all-our-homework-to-get-eu-candidate-status-kosovo-s-pm-albin-kurti" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24 hosts Albin Kurti, the prime minister of Kosovo, a country that declared its independence from Serbia back in 2008 and sees itself as part of the European family. But four years after applying to join the EU, Kosovo has still not received candidate status. We explore Kosovo's path towards the EU, and the broader European and regional dynamics surrounding that.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>As EU grapples with fierce AI competition, summit overshadowed by elusive Ukraine-Russia peace deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:897942fbbf95d2cd2a9548e4442d96ed02e91282dcac4c057354798c525f9015</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:28:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-as-eu-grapples-with-fierce-ai-competition-summit-overshadowed-by-elusive-ukraine-russia-pea--d418c75912c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-as-eu-grapples-with-fierce-ai-competition-summit-overshadowed-by-elusive-ukraine-russia-peace-deal-1" /><summary type="html">As EU leaders meet for an AI summit in Dublin, largely overshadowed by Russia's war on Ukraine, William Hilderbrandt is pleased to welcome Fabrice Pothier, CEO of Rasmussen Global. On AI, Pothier points to Europe's limited computing capacity, estimating that it barely represents "5% of what's available out there." Despite the EU's wealth of researchers and expertise, he warns that Europe is struggling to turn these resources into "real technological and industrial scale." Now, turning to the war in Ukraine, Pothier argues that European governments should focus less on "whether they have a place at the table" and more on "making Ukraine's hands stronger," particularly by providing additional air defence interceptors.</summary></entry><entry><title>The Nvidia affair: Are markets about to fall out of love with AI?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63f8c0fe2bed32b691d651b1a46a3f3b7f8c17064598a7aa7c73d87c5437a013</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:02:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-the-nvidia-affair-are-markets-about-to-fall-out-of-love-with-ai--afdd33fb8417.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-the-nvidia-affair-are-markets-about-to-fall-out-of-love-with-ai" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang’s departure from Nvidia exposes the vulnerabilities behind the AI boom. As equities reel in response to his resignation following extramarital affairs, alleged Chinese espionage and a summons to testify before US lawmakers, questions mount over who is really in charge of tech and whether the immense capital riding on it can survive the turmoil.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>November 13 Paris attacks: Eleven years later, France pays tribute to victims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d78d91ff1e420c257277b1b149f9ca26b063c4896ac52f6cc8f624d2e21af898</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:47:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/november-13-paris-attacks-eleven-years-later-france-pays-tribute-to-victims--43a7704539a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/november-13-paris-attacks-eleven-years-later-france-pays-tribute-to-victims" /><summary type="html">Eleven years on, France pays tribute to the victims of the November 13 attacks. French officials, victims’ associations and families gathered this Friday to pay their respects to those killed in the attacks in Paris on November 13, 2015.</summary></entry><entry><title>Crossing Afghanistan along the 'highway of death'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:751e008a83ecc0a379a4554b81e8f90cc0fdd94543fe390ab871a83b0e35ead5</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:47:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261113-crossing-afghanistan-along-the-highway-of-death--fa8fa1756aea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261113-crossing-afghanistan-along-the-highway-of-death" /><summary type="html">Highway 1, or the Ring Road, connects Afghanistan's major cities. After September 11, 2001, it became a hotspot for crime and fighting, particularly between the capital Kabul and Kandahar, the Taliban's birthplace. People taking it had to navigate extortions, kidnappings and suicide bombings. What has become of the road after the US-led war and five years of Taliban rule? Our former Afghanistan correspondent Claire Billet and photojournalist Sandra Calligaro returned to the country to find out.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Junta carries out double-tap airstrikes targeting civilians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d845d0c1e30abeb3811cc72f576c6234ae4a5cd89bd9d4db78be9763d137589e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:41:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261113-myanmar-junta-airstrikes-civilians--249ccb264ea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261113-myanmar-junta-airstrikes-civilians" /><summary type="html">Numerous civilian casualties have been documented in Rakhine State amid a renewed military offensive by the junta to regain control of the area.  Available evidence suggests that military aircraft are deliberately targeting civilian sites and carrying out double-tap strikes.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>El Niño fuels climate disasters: The high price of inaction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93792791f9d97c90911d783dca5cdb8e7ee09c81cb4b4af95a8d19708471ec16</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:35:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261113-el-ni_o-fuels-climate-disasters-the-high-price-of-inaction--5caf5eedf5ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261113-el-ni%C3%B1o-fuels-climate-disasters-the-high-price-of-inaction" /><summary type="html">2026 is set to be one of the hottest years on record, with El Niño worsening the impact of extreme weather events. With COP31 underway in Turkey, FRANCE 24 speaks with the UNDP's climate boss about the cost of waiting in a warmer world, and with one of the student activists from Pacific Island nations who took their climate fight to the UN's highest court, and won.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: ‘Without international trade and financial support, large settlements would not exist’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b380757c1586d9b5b7f12271b51182b4d0afd419fd1dc9786a4570527eda7904</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:15:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exi--ca01d4fe66ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exist-1" /><summary type="html">France is considering legislation to restrict trade with Israeli settlements in the occupied Palestinian territories, namely the West Bank. Ivar Ekeland, Professor Emeritus at Paris Dauphine-PSL University and Chair of the Organization of Academics for the Respect of International Law in Palestine, discusses the proposed measures with Alison Sargent. He calls for restrictions to cover n ot only goods but also services, including financial services, insurance and tourism. "Without the support of financial entities, of insurance, of providing goods and so on, settlements, big settlements, would not exist," he argues.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN refugee chief Barham Salih slams 'shameful' war in Sudan, urges 'political solution'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1a160aa18014ecdeea20c8e1272e775a192c11986228870d4f086c63a0e6b6b</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:56:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261113-un-refugee-chief-barham-salih-slams-shameful-war-in-sudan-urges-political-solution--a499e7d27829.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261113-un-refugee-chief-barham-salih-slams-shameful-war-in-sudan-urges-political-solution" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, UN refugee chief Barham Salih called the war in Sudan "shameful" and urged the world to end it. With forced displacement at a record high, he warned that funding cuts are hurting people "in dire need". "Efficiency has its limits," he said. Salih also defended the "integrity of the asylum system".</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>France asks Brussels to examine Algeria's non-compliance of EU association agreement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa76bd59ae266fdc3e2da0fd09431490487eab9195863e217de985a01b467b79</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:54:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261113-france-asks-brussels-to-examine-algeria-s-non-compliance-of-eu-association-agreement--930580abb7b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261113-france-asks-brussels-to-examine-algeria-s-non-compliance-of-eu-association-agreement" /><summary type="html">France announced on Friday that it will ask the European Commission to "examine" Algeria's non-compliance with its EU association agreement. Earlier in July, Algiers imposed a near-blanket ban on French imports, and last month, Algeria suspended urea shipments to France.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia scandal: How close was ex-CEO to Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b08da3024459391f9eef11a19c6fe762ff75bf3d05c964739af34b99ebddd75</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:50:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-nvidia-scandal-how-close-was-ex-ceo-to-trump--b0c156ec823c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-nvidia-scandal-how-close-was-ex-ceo-to-trump" /><summary type="html">US lawmakers have called Jensen Huang to face their questions in December after the Nvidia ex-CEO quit over extramarital affairs, including one with a suspected Chinese spy. The Taiwanese-born businessman was a close informal adviser to President Donald Trump on AI and had spent years lobbying against curbs on sales of advanced AI chips to China for national security reasons. Just how close Huang was to Trump and the extent of the influence tech giants have on his administration are some of the questions that still need answering, says France 24’s Douglas Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes targets across Ukraine as Kyiv launches nearly 1,200 drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f52b74704429e76be950d40e4912a25d129c16192e52d3a80d7fc40a6579906</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:46:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-russian-airstrikes-continue-ukraine-launches-nearly-1-200-drones--8c91678fb217.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-russian-airstrikes-continue-ukraine-launches-nearly-1-200-drones" /><summary type="html">Russian strikes hit targets across Ukraine on Thursday, with one attack damaging a hospital. Ukraine meanwhile fired almost 1,200 drones at Russian targets overnight in one of its biggest aerial attacks since Moscow’s full-scale invasion nearly five years ago.</summary></entry><entry><title>Haitian forces recapture national stadium after two years of gang control</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36cdb9fbb718ccbe2111976600446268f2bde7ca98907ba60387b062ed9fb39d</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:09:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-haitian-forces-recapture-national-stadium-after-two-years-of-gang-control--cac3a4adff3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-haitian-forces-recapture-national-stadium-after-two-years-of-gang-control" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces regained control Thursday, November 12, of the country's main stadium that had been under gang control for two years, forcing the national football team to play elsewhere. The Haitian National Police said in a statement that it had taken "full control" of the venue with the Task Force, a private security group serving the government, after which it left the stadium under the guard of Salvadoran soldiers.</summary></entry></feed>
